                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd3343c1-fd60-371d-adb7-d706bfd30d84",
                                        "entry_id": "b64985d9-459f-360a-8af7-c7cbc903cc6e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to pulp magazines; in the style of a pulp magazine or the material printed within such a publication."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20e67b32-146c-431d-be9a-f2fcd85c2cff",
                                                "sense_id": "fd3343c1-fd60-371d-adb7-d706bfd30d84",
                                                "text": "The Nightwing annual had what felt like a very 'pulp-ish' plot, and the Superman annual was great, with a very pulp plot and a^([sic]) incredible Doc Savage tribute cover."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a89cdc8c-64ab-46ea-9315-a1288bcd19d8",
                                                "sense_id": "fd3343c1-fd60-371d-adb7-d706bfd30d84",
                                                "text": "Rather than Asimov I might suggest Stanley Weinbaum (since he died young and early in his career, he is far more \"pulp\" than Asimov - and remarkably readable - there is a LANCER collection of some of his short stories)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "17dee847-0b24-403f-a178-c5d54b6d758c",
